{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 11, "model_name": "nvidia/llama-3.3-nemotron-super-49b-v1", "content": "i recently watched the movie \"the social network\" and here is my detailed review in all lower case as requested:\n\n**movie title:** the social network\n**director:** david fincher\n**release year:** 2010\n**genre:** biography, drama\n\n**summary:**\nthe movie tells the story of how facebook came into existence, focusing on the founder mark zuckerberg and the controversies surrounding its creation. the film explores the journey from its humble beginnings as a college project to becoming a global phenomenon, intertwined with the legal battles and personal relationships that suffered as a consequence.\n\n**acting:**\n- jesse eisenberg as mark zuckerberg gives a compelling performance, capturing the intensity and brilliance of the character.\n- andrew garfield as eduard savarain (co-founder and initial investor) portrays the emotional depth and betrayal felt during the fallout with zuckerberg.\n- justin timberlake as sean parker (co-founder of napster) brings a charismatic energy to the film, influencing the direction of facebook significantly.\n\n**direction and cinematography:**\ndavid fincher's direction is impeccable, weaving a complex narrative with ease. the cinematography is sleek, mirroring the tech-driven world the characters inhabit. the use of lighting and camera angles enhances the mood of each scene, from the intense coding nights to the dramatic courtroom sessions.\n\n**script:**\naaron sorkin's script is razor-sharp, with dialogue that is both witty and revealing of the characters' depths. the non-linear storytelling keeps the viewer engaged, jumping between the formation of facebook and the legal proceedings against zuckerberg.\n\n**music:**\ntrent reznor and atticus ross's soundtrack is hauntingly beautiful, perfectly complementing the on-screen tension and emotional highs and lows.\n\n**critique:**\n- while the movie is well-researched, some liberties are taken with the true events, which might not entirely please everyone involved in the real story.\n- the pacing, although generally well-managed, might feel a bit rushed in certain plot transitions.\n\n**rating:** 4.5/5\n\n**recommendation:**\nthe social network is a must-watch for anyone interested in the tech world, entrepreneurship, or compelling character studies. despite its minor flaws, the movie offers a deeply engaging viewing experience.\n\n**final thoughts:**\nthe social network is not just a movie about facebook; it's a commentary on ambition, friendship, and the consequences of success. it leaves the viewer with a lot to ponder long after the credits roll.", "logprobs": [{"token": "i", "logprob": -0.04083649069070816}, {"token": " recently", "logprob": -1.5719144344329834}, {"token": " watched", "logprob": -0.17987512052059174}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.4827228784561157}, {"token": " movie", "logprob": -0.0003182381624355912}, {"token": " \"", "logprob": -0.00011526874004630372}, {"token": "the", "logprob": -4.768370445162873e-07}, {"token": " social", "logprob": -4.768370445162873e-07}, {"token": " network", "logprob": -3.4570634852570947e-06}, {"token": "\"", "logprob": -0.00437505217269063}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.011181431822478771}, {"token": " here", "logprob": -0.11195193976163864}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.14721544086933136}, {"token": " my", "logprob": -0.00043108707177452743}, {"token": " detailed", "logprob": -1.3351351299206726e-05}, {"token": " review", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": " in", "logprob": -0.010511391796171665}, {"token": " all", "logprob": -0.0017406088300049305}, {"token": " lower", "logprob": -0.014176259748637676}, {"token": " case", "logprob": -2.861018856492592e-06}, {"token": " as", "logprob": -0.13015325367450714}, {"token": " requested", "logprob": -0.004079235717654228}, {"token": ":\n\n", "logprob": -0.01111777313053608}, {"token": "**", "logprob": 